{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting","id":232755,"title":"Awkward Questions about Lunar Shapeshifting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-18T06:00:43-07:00","id":232755,"title":"Awkward Questions about Lunar Shapeshifting","content":"...because I'm bored, and boredom justifies all things.<br /> <br /> 1. If a Lunar gets impregnated in the form of a mammal (not a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monotreme\" target=\"_blank\">monotreme</a>), and then turns into a bird or reptile, will she lay eggs? If so, what will hatch from those eggs?<br /> <br /> 2. If a Lunar gets impregnated in the form of a reptile or bird, and then turns into a mammal (not a monotreme), will she give live birth? If so, what will she give birth to?<br /> <br /> 3. If a Lunar eats something that would be poisonous to a human (e.g. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phytolacca_americana\" target=\"_blank\">Pokeweed</a>) while in the form of something that can eat them (like a bird), and then changes forms before digesting, will they get poisoned?<br /> <br /> 4. If a hungry Lunar takes the form of something very large (like a Tyrant Lizard), then eats something larger than a human (like a cow), and then turns into a human, will they explode?<br /> <br /> 5. If a hungry Lunar takes the form of something very small, eats a meal appropriate to the size of that creature, and then turns back into a human, will they still be hungry?<br /> <br /> 6. How do you calculate damage for being swallowed in the form of something small, and then transforming into something large?<br /> <br /> 7. What kind of powers would you associate with a Lunar that has a platypus as a spirit totem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T06:04:15-07:00","id":232776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of powers would you associate with a Lunar that has a platypus as a spirit totem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Transcendent Perception and poison Charms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T07:00:53-07:00","id":232796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...because I'm bored, and boredom justifies all things.<br /> <br /> 1. If a Lunar gets impregnated in the form of a mammal (not a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monotreme\" target=\"_blank\">monotreme</a>), and then turns into a bird or reptile, will she lay eggs? If so, what will hatch from those eggs?<br /> <br /> 2. If a Lunar gets impregnated in the form of a reptile or bird, and then turns into a mammal (not a monotreme), will she give live birth? If so, what will she give birth to?<br /> <br /> 3. If a Lunar eats something that would be poisonous to a human (e.g. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phytolacca_americana\" target=\"_blank\">Pokeweed</a>) while in the form of something that can eat them (like a bird), and then changes forms before digesting, will they get poisoned?<br /> <br /> 4. If a hungry Lunar takes the form of something very large (like a Tyrant Lizard), then eats something larger than a human (like a cow), and then turns into a human, will they explode?<br /> <br /> 5. If a hungry Lunar takes the form of something very small, eats a meal appropriate to the size of that creature, and then turns back into a human, will they still be hungry?<br /> <br /> 6. How do you calculate damage for being swallowed in the form of something small, and then transforming into something large?<br /> <br /> 7. What kind of powers would you associate with a Lunar that has a platypus as a spirit totem?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Obviously this is just GM ruling, and will vary between person to person. Here would be my &quot;rulings.&quot;<br /> <br /> 1+2 The method of birth will revert to human method, even if it doesn't make biological sense.<br /> --Exception: Totem true form may substituted by the Lunar at will.<br /> --2nd Exception: If the Lunar has breeding charms, they have more control over what happens.<br /> <br /> 3. Once the plant has been ingested, it has become overwhelmed by the Lunar's natural essence, and so does not poison them.<br /> -- Exception: Anything with an &quot;essence rating&quot;--such as something magical, wyld tainted, Exalt-crafted, etc. may &quot;contest&quot; this.<br /> <br /> 4. No, the extra food is &quot;magically digested.&quot; It does mean the Lunar can binge eat and feel full for the next few days, as it is &quot;rationed&quot; out to natural energy requirements of his true form.<br /> <br /> 5. The Lunar will become hungry soon. When they are a mouse, they can eat mouse-sized meals, but when they shapeshift back the &quot;energy&quot; stored in their essence flows will quickly be consumed at the rate of their true form. This is true for a large form: they are required to eat more to continually sustain as they burn more energy.<br /> <br /> 6. I know it's kinda weird, but I would use the grapple rules for &quot;can this contain her as she's growing?&quot;, and then solid strength damage for &quot;bursting out&quot;<br /> <br /> 7. Get that Lunar tattooed cause she has OBVIOUSLY been Wyld-tainted!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T07:11:46-07:00","id":232802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. If a Lunar gets impregnated in the form of a mammal (not a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monotreme\" target=\"_blank\">monotreme</a>), and then turns into a bird or reptile, will she lay eggs? If so, what will hatch from those eggs?</div> </div> </div> </div>If she is big enough to lay an egg containing the mammal, I would go with the mammal (because that would make for some disturbing scenes), but without a navel obviously. If she is laying small eggs, then it will probably be a tiny dead human inside.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. If a Lunar gets impregnated in the form of a reptile or bird, and then turns into a mammal (not a monotreme), will she give live birth? If so, what will she give birth to?</div> </div> </div> </div>If she is big enough, she will give birth to a reptile or bird. With a navel. If she is too small, when giving birth, it will be a tiny dead version.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. If a Lunar eats something that would be poisonous to a human (e.g. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phytolacca_americana\" target=\"_blank\">Pokeweed</a>) while in the form of something that can eat them (like a bird), and then changes forms before digesting, will they get poisoned?</div> </div> </div> </div>This would make for some really silly scenes, so I would say no.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. If a hungry Lunar takes the form of something very large (like a Tyrant Lizard), then eats something larger than a human (like a cow), and then turns into a human, will they explode?</div> </div> </div> </div>Too silly for me. I would say no.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. If a hungry Lunar takes the form of something very small, eats a meal appropriate to the size of that creature, and then turns back into a human, will they still be hungry?</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot come up with a satifying answer for this one.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. How do you calculate damage for being swallowed in the form of something small, and then transforming into something large?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a storyteller, I would say that if you come up with this tactic on the fly when someone intentionally eats you, you get to do it without any damage. If you turn into a fly and intentionally flies into someone's mouth, you take all the damage. All of it.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7. What kind of powers would you associate with a Lunar that has a platypus as a spirit totem?</div> </div> </div> </div>What is it... beaks, claws, poisonous stinger...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T07:19:18-07:00","id":232807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=232802#post232802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is it... beaks, claws, poisonous stinger...</div> </div> </div> </div>The beak is electroreceptive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T07:27:36-07:00","id":232811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. If a Lunar gets impregnated in the form of a mammal (not a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monotreme\" target=\"_blank\">monotreme</a>), and then turns into a bird or reptile, will she lay eggs? If so, what will hatch from those eggs?<br /> <br /> 2. If a Lunar gets impregnated in the form of a reptile or bird, and then turns into a mammal (not a monotreme), will she give live birth? If so, what will she give birth to?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW, your children's mutations depend only on the form you were in during their conception. Further shapeshifting after that point has no effect on what they become. That implies your womb stays the same until you give birth, but there's no rule that it has to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. If a hungry Lunar takes the form of something very large (like a Tyrant Lizard), then eats something larger than a human (like a cow), and then turns into a human, will they explode?<br /> <br /> 5. If a hungry Lunar takes the form of something very small, eats a meal appropriate to the size of that creature, and then turns back into a human, will they still be hungry?</div> </div> </div> </div>No and no. Shapeshifting doesn't damage the clothes you're wearing, so it shouldn't damage the food you've eaten. If you need to track your biological process that precisely, I'd say whatever you're in the process of digesting counts as part of your essence once it's dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of powers would you associate with a Lunar that has a platypus as a spirit totem?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't know. High Perception. War form might have <i>shark sight</i> mutation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T07:39:18-07:00","id":232818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=232802#post232802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a storyteller, I would say that if you come up with this tactic on the fly when someone intentionally eats you, you get to do it without any damage. If you turn into a fly and intentionally flies into someone's mouth, you take all the damage. All of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this question was meant as asking how to calculate damage done to the one that ate the Lunar, not damage done <i>to</i> the Lunar. Nothing can prevent a Lunar from shapeshifting, and I'd imagine that the number of beings able to survive a tyrant lizard chestburster are rather small.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T08:05:14-07:00","id":232833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=232818#post232818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this question was meant as asking how to calculate damage done to the one that ate the Lunar, not damage done <i>to</i> the Lunar. Nothing can prevent a Lunar from shapeshifting, and I'd imagine that the number of beings able to survive a tyrant lizard chestburster are rather small.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of goes both ways, really. I think it would be reasonable for the Lunar to take Bashing damage from being crushed by the whatever they're trying to chestburst out of, depending on what ate them and what they're turning into. Could lead to an incredibly gruesome and morbidly hilarious death for both participants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:08:12-07:00","id":232883,"title":"","content":"Not sure what powers the platypus would have, but socially, I bet a few people would be concerned about Chimerism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:20:55-07:00","id":232897,"title":"","content":"Native to the western bordermarches, on the lost island of Oztreyliar, where the wildlife almost invariably shows signs of Wyld taint. The platypus is a rather extreme example, being some sort of mutant beaver-duck, but it is relatively harmless and tolerated in most societies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:28:21-07:00","id":232902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=232883#post232883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what powers the platypus would have, but socially, I bet a few people would be concerned about Chimerism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This &quot;joke&quot; needs to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:54:53-07:00","id":232921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...because I'm bored, and boredom justifies all things.<br /> <br /> 1. If a Lunar gets impregnated in the form of a mammal (not a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monotreme\" target=\"_blank\">monotreme</a>), and then turns into a bird or reptile, will she lay eggs? If so, what will hatch from those eggs?<br /> <br /> 2. If a Lunar gets impregnated in the form of a reptile or bird, and then turns into a mammal (not a monotreme), will she give live birth? If so, what will she give birth to?</div> </div> </div> </div>You tell me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. If a Lunar eats something that would be poisonous to a human (e.g. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phytolacca_americana\" target=\"_blank\">Pokeweed</a>) while in the form of something that can eat them (like a bird), and then changes forms before digesting, will they get poisoned? </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Realistically, it's possible. Game-wise, no Storyteller should ever have to track digestion times, so no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. If a hungry Lunar takes the form of something very large (like a Tyrant Lizard), then eats something larger than a human (like a cow), and then turns into a human, will they explode?<br /> <br /> 5. If a hungry Lunar takes the form of something very small, eats a meal appropriate to the size of that creature, and then turns back into a human, will they still be hungry? </div> </div> </div>Something something Elsewhere displacement something something Essence something something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. How do you calculate damage for being swallowed in the form of something small, and then transforming into something large? </div> </div> </div>I'd probably resolve that as a type of stunted grapple. If you don't roll enough damage to kill them (albeit I'd be giving you a bonus), you either can't transform yet, or do so in a way that doesn't involve a chestburster. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. What kind of powers would you associate with a Lunar that has a platypus as a spirit totem? </div> </div> </div>Electroreceptivity, poisonous spurs, aquatic mobility, webbed feet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:12:42-07:00","id":233125,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd say that transforming back while swallowed just does a bit of bashing damage while the person or animal uncomfortably coughs you back up.<br /> <br /> And that oddities in birthing or hatching are like neomah babies or Oathchildren; they're mostly normal examples of the relevant species, just with a few oddities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:25:07-07:00","id":233141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=232921#post232921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably resolve that as a type of stunted grapple. If you don't roll enough damage to kill them (albeit I'd be giving you a bonus), you either can't transform yet, or do so in a way that doesn't involve a chestburster.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you transform but it doesn't kill them outright, honestly, that's hardly looking any better for them. Because having a live burrow lok in your stomach is no fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-18-2014, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:37:48-07:00","id":233150,"title":"","content":"Yeah, shapeshifting over 5 ticks would probably be enough time to cough/vomit the thing back up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But what about that knack that allows you to shapeshift at Reflexive speed (Lightning Change Mastery I think.. or Style?) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:05:16-07:00","id":233173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting#post232755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...because I'm bored, and boredom justifies all things.<br /> <br /> 1. If a Lunar gets impregnated in the form of a mammal (not a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monotreme\" target=\"_blank\">monotreme</a>), and then turns into a bird or reptile, will she lay eggs? If so, what will hatch from those eggs?<br /> <br /> 2. If a Lunar gets impregnated in the form of a reptile or bird, and then turns into a mammal (not a monotreme), will she give live birth? If so, what will she give birth to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that for these two questions in particular, we should defer to the timeless wisdom of Rumiko Takahashi re: Ranma Saotome and the logistics of reproduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:07:19-07:00","id":233175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233173#post233173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that for these two questions in particular, we should defer to the timeless wisdom of Rumiko Takahashi re: Ranma Saotome and the logistics of reproduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understandable, but &quot;I haven't thought about that, and you shouldn't either&quot; is a train of thought I like to see applied sparingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:08:40-07:00","id":233177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233173#post233173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that for these two questions in particular, we should defer to the timeless wisdom of Rumiko Takahashi re: Ranma Saotome and the logistics of reproduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I don't think about that, and neither should you?&quot;<br /> <br /> Too late for that, I'm afraid. Just be thankful none of my questions involve gender-swapping.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:50:06-07:00","id":233201,"title":"","content":"Presumably they'd just do what Luna does and keep the womb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:58:10-07:00","id":233206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233150#post233150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, shapeshifting over 5 ticks would probably be enough time to cough/vomit the thing back up.<br /> <br /> But what about that knack that allows you to shapeshift at Reflexive speed (Lightning Change Mastery I think.. or Style?) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shapeshifting counts as instantaneous even without those knacks. Its Speed determines when you can next act after shapeshifting, but the change itself is effective immediately.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=232921#post232921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably resolve that as a type of stunted grapple. If you don't roll enough damage to kill them (albeit I'd be giving you a bonus), you either can't transform yet, or do so in a way that doesn't involve a chestburster.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>No known physical or magical force can prevent one of Luna\u2019s Children from shifting shape. If a Steward chooses to wear a different form and it lies within her power, she can take the action to change, even when magic constrains her from taking any action at all.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-18-2014, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:29:57-07:00","id":233247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233173#post233173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that for these two questions in particular, we should defer to the timeless wisdom of Rumiko Takahashi re: Ranma Saotome and the logistics of reproduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that there was an arc that involved water of permanence that kept up Curse Transformations, so she clearly did think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:47:26-07:00","id":233263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233247#post233247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that there was an arc that involved water of permanence that kept up Curse Transformations, so she clearly did think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will preface this question by noting I haven't thought about Ranma in a very long time and may not have ever seen/read that arc. Are you sure direct implications of pregnancy logistics were referenced? I mean, water that makes a Jusenkyo curse into a permanent state is going to be obviously undesirable to most. Mousse and Ryoga would be at least as terrified of the prospect as Ranma. Unless the purposes of pregnancy were actually mentioned -- and meant as more than a throwaway joke -- I'm not inclined to read much into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:26:27-07:00","id":233334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233263#post233263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will preface this question by noting I haven't thought about Ranma in a very long time and may not have ever seen/read that arc. Are you sure direct implications of pregnancy logistics were referenced? I mean, water that makes a Jusenkyo curse into a permanent state is going to be obviously undesirable to most. Mousse and Ryoga would be at least as terrified of the prospect as Ranma. Unless the purposes of pregnancy were actually mentioned -- and meant as more than a throwaway joke -- I'm not inclined to read much into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, in that case it was &quot;turn a monkey/tiger/dragon/whatevs into a human girl, formlock, make with the babies, children carry slight aesthetic traits of non-human parent.&quot; The idea of that happening to Ranma was never explored.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:04:35-07:00","id":233368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233206#post233206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>No known physical or magical force can prevent one of Luna\u2019s Children from shifting shape. If a Steward chooses to wear a different form and it lies within her power, she can take the action to change, even when magic constrains her from taking any action at all.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The Storyteller is not a physical or magical force. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:28:19-07:00","id":233387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233206#post233206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shapeshifting counts as instantaneous even without those knacks. Its Speed determines when you can next act after shapeshifting, but the change itself is effective immediately.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>No known physical or magical force can prevent one of Luna\u2019s Children from shifting shape. If a Steward chooses to wear a different form and it lies within her power, she can take the action to change, even when magic constrains her from taking any action at all.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's that whole known thing right there you gotta aim at. Just because there's nothing anyone knows about that can do it doesn't mean there can't be. Just that as soon as the ST puts it in play be prepared for the players to weaponize it if they can get some too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:28:20-07:00","id":233388,"title":"","content":"Right, okay.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.chrysander.com/lebowski/walter_rules.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:31:33-07:00","id":233391,"title":"","content":"Just have them vomited out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:34:10-07:00","id":233395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233388#post233388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, okay.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.chrysander.com/lebowski/walter_rules.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.chrysander.com/lebowski/walter_rules.jpg</a></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ea3BJCksGJ4\" data-code=\"Ea3BJCksGJ4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Ea3BJCksGJ4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> One potential balancing point for large forms is, perhaps, not being able to assume them without enough room to do so. This also makes small forms advantageous in cramped quarters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:56:52-07:00","id":233443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233388#post233388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, okay.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.chrysander.com/lebowski/walter_rules.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Turn into a fly, go up someone's nostril, shapeshift into a tyrant lizard&quot; is not a combat strategy that produces fun gameplay. A Storyteller's job is to produce fun gameplay. Sometimes, rules are unfortunately not helpful to them in this job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:02:11-07:00","id":233470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233443#post233443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Turn into a fly, go up someone's nostril, shapeshift into a tyrant lizard&quot; is not a combat strategy that produces fun gameplay. A Storyteller's job is to produce fun gameplay. Sometimes, rules are unfortunately not helpful to them in this job.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It'd be fun the first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:07:03-07:00","id":233482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233443#post233443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Turn into a fly, go up someone's nostril, shapeshift into a tyrant lizard&quot; is not a combat strategy that produces fun gameplay. A Storyteller's job is to produce fun gameplay. Sometimes, rules are unfortunately not helpful to them in this job.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Lunar in whatever form is already inside your body, it's pretty much all over for you whether the Lunar can shapeshift or not. Claws of the Silver Moon is all that would be needed to give you a gruesome death. It's an easily exploitable scenario, but you're not going to fix it by saying there's no shapeshifting inside a cramped space. Better to just agree with your players not to exploit their abilities that way because it's not fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:07:37-07:00","id":233483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233470#post233470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It'd be fun the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool if it's a thing that can be done. Like, that is clever use of shapeshifting, and I would be sad if the rules were ever just NO IMPOSSIBLE.<br /> <br /> At the same time, if Lunars have an instant-kill strategy that requires no combat investment, two Knacks, works on anyone who doesn't have superhuman senses, costs very little, and is easy to perform, that is not fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:24:02-07:00","id":233496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233483#post233483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's cool if it's a thing that can be done. Like, that is clever use of shapeshifting, and I would be sad if the rules were ever just NO IMPOSSIBLE.<br /> <br /> At the same time, if Lunars have an instant-kill strategy that requires no combat investment, two Knacks, works on anyone who doesn't have superhuman senses, costs very little, and is easy to perform, that is not fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>If done with frequency, I'd imagine that it would prompt the forging of razored jade flyswatters and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:00:42-07:00","id":233530,"title":"","content":"You can have people vomit/sneeze/cough them out automatically, and if the Lunar wants to stay inside, they need to do an appropriate stunt or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:13:12-07:00","id":233552,"title":"","content":"Oh Nash Equilibrium, how fragile you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:36:06-07:00","id":233627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233482#post233482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Lunar in whatever form is already inside your body, it's pretty much all over for you whether the Lunar can shapeshift or not. Claws of the Silver Moon is all that would be needed to give you a gruesome death. It's an easily exploitable scenario, but you're not going to fix it by saying there's no shapeshifting inside a cramped space. Better to just agree with your players not to exploit their abilities that way because it's not fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are going to get very, very bad results in the long term if you allow getting inside an enemy's body to be an instant victory for a Lunar. This is the kind of thing that tests a GM's ability to improvise rules that are functional while also leading the game in a good direction, and making it so that is a reliable way to kill someone is not the latter even if it is the former.<br /> <br /> Of course, this does work better if the system isn't built for rocket tag from the ground up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:07:51-07:00","id":233666,"title":"","content":"See I'm fine with the idea of&quot; The tyrant lizard ate me and so I turned into an elephant because I wasn't getting out through my own power and I figured at least the elephant wouldn't slide down into the stomach easily.&quot; But like hell am I allowing dnd's spelunker build to become a standard battle tactic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":".  Fixing a spelling error 08-24-2014, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:37:33-07:00","id":233703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233482#post233482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Lunar in whatever form is already inside your body, it's pretty much all over for you whether the Lunar can shapeshift or not. Claws of the Silver Moon is all that would be needed to give you a gruesome death. It's an easily exploitable scenario, but you're not going to fix it by saying there's no shapeshifting inside a cramped space. Better to just agree with your players not to exploit their abilities that way because it's not fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Big ol' middle being excluded. &quot;Changing Faces, Cramped Spaces&quot; would be like, a paragraph-long sidebar to write, if there were to be a book on Lunars being written in the near future, and even just running 2e, I think you could kitbash a quick and dirty way of handling it that isn't just &quot;instant death&quot; or &quot;nope, let's not do that.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:41:42-07:00","id":233707,"title":"","content":"What is a kitbash?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:44:28-07:00","id":233713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233703#post233703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big ol' middle being excluded. &quot;Changing Faces, Cramped Spaces&quot; would be like, a paragraph-long sidebar to write, if there were to be a book on Lunars being written in the near future, and even just running 2e, I think you could kitbash a quick and dirty way of handling it that isn't just &quot;instant death&quot; or &quot;nope, let's not do that.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233627#post233627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are going to get very, very bad results in the long term if you allow getting inside an enemy's body to be an instant victory for a Lunar. This is the kind of thing that tests a GM's ability to improvise rules that are functional while also leading the game in a good direction, and making it so that is a reliable way to kill someone is not the latter even if it is the former.<br /> <br /> Of course, this does work better if the system isn't built for rocket tag from the ground up.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, what's funny to me is that I don't think anyone on this thread was actually aware, until I pointed it out, that no known force in Creation, Hell or Heaven can prevent a Lunar from changing shape. Not orichalcum chains, not sorcery, not the Yozi Isidoros straining every muscle in his body until his veins go pop. That's kind of awesome IMO. And it's a pretty basic and important fact about Lunar shapeshifting, and you'd think people would be aware of it, but no one mentioned it until I did, and I don't think anyone was going to because no one actually knew the rules. That's how it usually works. I point out how the game works, and then I get dogpiled by people who insist I'm doing it wrong.<br /> <br /> If you want to tell your players they have to win a grapple in order to shapeshift, go for it. All I'm saying it that's not normally how it works. And it doesn't solve the problem anyway; a Lunar already inside someone's body has plenty of options for killing them besides shapeshifting. If you need a solution, personally I'd be more inclined to go with Hippokrene's, since it doesn't involve overt fucking with Lunar powers, but then I've never had to deal with this kind of abusive scenario in a game and I don't think I ever will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-19-2014, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:45:19-07:00","id":233716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233707#post233707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is a kitbash?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, &quot;there's no rules for this, we're running the game live, I'm gonna jigger up some rolls for the player to make so that fun can happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it goes back to minis games originally, were you use like, leftover bits of Warhammer figurines or whatever to do stuff, but that is not my jam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:46:14-07:00","id":233720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233707#post233707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is a kitbash?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> a kibosh? Put an end to decisively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:49:23-07:00","id":233724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233713#post233713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to tell your players they have to win a grapple in order to shapeshift, go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm too lazy to go back and look, but I don't think anyone <i>has</i> said that. I mostly remember people saying, &quot;You have to win a grapple in order for that shapeshifting you described to do what you want it to do.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:50:04-07:00","id":233725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233713#post233713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, what's funny to me is that I don't think anyone on this thread was actually aware, until I pointed it out, that no known force in Creation, Hell or Heaven can prevent a Lunar from changing shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except spending a few too many motes, of course.<br /> <br /> Isidoros, no. Actually use your Peripheral Essence pool, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 08-18-2014, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:50:58-07:00","id":233726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233724#post233724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm too lazy to go back and look, but I don't think anyone <i>has</i> said that. I mostly remember people saying, &quot;You have to win a grapple in order for that shapeshifting you described to do what you want it to do.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Found it for you:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=232921#post232921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably resolve that as a type of stunted grapple. If you don't roll enough damage... <b>you either can't transform yet,</b> or do so in a way that doesn't involve a chestburster.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:56:32-07:00","id":233729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233713#post233713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, what's funny to me is that I don't think anyone on this thread was actually aware, until I pointed it out, that no known force in Creation, Hell or Heaven can prevent a Lunar from changing shape. Not orichalcum chains, not sorcery, not the Yozi Isidoros straining every muscle in his body until his veins go pop. That's kind of awesome IMO. And it's a pretty basic and important fact about Lunar shapeshifting, and you'd think people would be aware of it, but no one mentioned it until I did, and I don't think anyone is going to because no one actually knew the rules. That's how it usually works. I point out how the game works, and in return I get dogpiled by people who insist I'm doing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of that rule. I did a lot of mechanics writing for late 2e, so, knowing how the rules work, a thing I am pretty okay at. Just because a rule is written does not mean that all situations produced by that rule are good, and boy does that come up in 2e a whole damn lot. I'm not trying to dogpile you; I have no dog in the race, let alone a pile. Just thought aloud about how I'd handle that situation in the hope that it would be helpful for other people trying to do the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:02:03-07:00","id":233735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233713#post233713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, what's funny to me is that I don't think anyone on this thread was actually aware, until I pointed it out, that no known force in Creation, Hell or Heaven can prevent a Lunar from changing shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an amazingly self-absorbed and arrogant attitude.<br /> <br /> We know what the books say. They've been saying it for the past twelve years. They also don't cover a large number of scenarios, like whether or not a Lunar could even fly into someone's nose in the first place (or other area). Those spaces are not usually wide open. They are usually shut tight by muscles. If it bothers you that much, assume that the clinch is to avoid letting the Lunar in, and use the statistics for the tiny, tiny form. Which, given its relative size, means that the Lunar isn't getting in, because I don't think that anything allowed by Emerald Grasshopper Form has even the slightest bit of quantifiable Strength. In fact, it could count as having negative Strength and give a bunch of bonus successes to the larger party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:15:51-07:00","id":233746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233726#post233726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Found it for you: <br /> &quot;Originally posted by <b>Robert Vance</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=232921#post232921\">View Post</a><br /> I'd probably resolve that as a type of stunted grapple. If you don't roll enough damage... <b>you either can't transform yet,</b> or do so in a way that doesn't involve a chestburster.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair that's how he's saying he would run it as a story teller. Which is perfectly viable. The other thing is as he points out in that you either don't go chestburster or you just can't shift yet, these are all very beneficial to the player in question. Another option would be that the space isn't big enough to allow you to shift in and since you don't put enough force in to break the space it holds stable against the transformation. Of course as you say nothing can stop that shift from taking place once it's happened so you will attempt to shift the structure around you will hold stable and you will die from being crushed to death as your body gets forced into an ever less appropriate fit. (Showed that flea formed dragon in dnd who's boss :P)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:33:00-07:00","id":233780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233746#post233746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair that's how he's saying he would run it as a story teller. Which is perfectly viable. The other thing is as he points out in that you either don't go chestburster or you just can't shift yet, these are all very beneficial to the player in question. Another option would be that the space isn't big enough to allow you to shift in and since you don't put enough force in to break the space it holds stable against the transformation. Of course as you say nothing can stop that shift from taking place once it's happened so you will attempt to shift the structure around you will hold stable and you will die from being crushed to death as your body gets forced into an ever less appropriate fit. (Showed that flea formed dragon in dnd who's boss :P)</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the shapeshifting could simply move you outside the person's body since there's not enough space inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:46:44-07:00","id":233810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233729#post233729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am aware of that rule. I did a lot of mechanics writing for late 2e, so, knowing how the rules work, a thing I am pretty okay at. Just because a rule is written does not mean that all situations produced by that rule are good, and boy does that come up in 2e a whole damn lot. I'm not trying to dogpile you; I have no dog in the race, let alone a pile. Just thought aloud about how I'd handle that situation in the hope that it would be helpful for other people trying to do the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such absolutes rarely work out anyway. I know of two ways in 2e just off the top of my head of ensuring that a lunar doesn't have the capacity to change forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:49:43-07:00","id":233815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233780#post233780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the shapeshifting could simply move you outside the person's body since there's not enough space inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Letting shapeshiting into a place you can't fit in your new shape function as a &quot;free&quot; Elsewhere jaunt is a bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:49:53-07:00","id":233816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233810#post233810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such absolutes rarely work out anyway. I know of two ways in 2e just off the top of my head of ensuring that a lunar doesn't have the capacity to change forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, one of them's gotta be Memory-Reweaving Discipline or something like that, but I'm blanking on what a second would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:51:45-07:00","id":233820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233815#post233815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Letting shapeshiting into a place you can't fit in your new shape function as a &quot;free&quot; Elsewhere jaunt is a bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does Elsewhere come into it?<br /> <br /> If you fly into a person's nostril and change shape, you don't need to pass through Elsewhere to end up outside their body. You just go out the body. Through the nose. Or the mouth, or whatever happens to be the closest orifice. There are more ways out of a human or animal body than moving magically through Elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:53:13-07:00","id":233821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233780#post233780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or the shapeshifting could simply move you outside the person's body since there's not enough space inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope I've checked with a few of my friends who DM and that came across as absurd to all of them. There's no precedent, there's no logic for it, and it removes a large number of penatlies for making a bad choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:01:37-07:00","id":233831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233816#post233816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, one of them's gotta be Memory-Reweaving Discipline or something like that, but I'm blanking on what a second would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any unnatural or natural mental influence that convinces a Lunar not to change shape, or being unconscious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:04:50-07:00","id":233837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233816#post233816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, one of them's gotta be Memory-Reweaving Discipline or something like that, but I'm blanking on what a second would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that's one that I didn't think of. The other two are an Abyssal trick and an Infernal trick respectively. There are soulsteel artifacts that allow you to drain and then continue to drain all essence. No essence to spend, no shapeshifting. <br /> <br /> The Infernal trick is based around the fact that Lunars have weak/few defenses against non-physical shaping. Kimbery's mutagenic poisons do a lovely job at giving people high power obsessions to do or not do something. Even more fun if one of those obsessions is to keep dosing themselves with potions/drugs that weaken the roll they'd have to take the action if someone UMI'd them into doing it.<br /> <br /> IIRC the punishment cage detailed in... Yu-shan book I think... might also drain all essence.... I'd have to check, it's been a while. I know it forces the victim to stay alive even if they're tortured to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:27:04-07:00","id":233868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233713#post233713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, what's funny to me is that I don't think anyone on this thread was actually aware, until I pointed it out, that no known force in Creation, Hell or Heaven can prevent a Lunar from changing shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, only you knew that.<br /> <br /> You special, special snowflake, you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233716#post233716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, &quot;there's no rules for this, we're running the game live, I'm gonna jigger up some rolls for the player to make so that fun can happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it goes back to minis games originally, were you use like, leftover bits of Warhammer figurines or whatever to do stuff, but that is not my jam.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:47:49-07:00","id":233882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233729#post233729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no dog in the race, let alone a pile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the puppy pile, of course!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:03:30-07:00","id":234097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233713#post233713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> You know, what's funny to me is that I don't think anyone on this thread was actually aware, until I pointed it out, that no known force in Creation, Hell or Heaven can prevent a Lunar from changing shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guys, we've gotta be careful; TSk is on the verge of figuring out that he's the only person who's ever actually played a Lunar.<br /> <br /> Wait... shit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:22:59-07:00","id":234121,"title":"","content":"I don't know what you're talking about; I..er... <i>totally</i> played Lunars before! Yeah!<br /> <br /> They're the ones that come from the Hedge and fight the Wyrm to protect the Graceful Wicked Masquerade, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T07:12:36-07:00","id":234157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233726#post233726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Found it for you:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, there it is. You are correct, and I'm wrong. Still, though, I can't be too impressed with the idea of following the rules no matter what; shit, Zeal was part of the rules no matter what, but anyone who told me I'm obligated to use it would get a slap across the face for his trouble. Or, to pick a less extreme example, the Jade Caste anima power is just plain worse than the Earth Aspect anima power, and probably costs more to activate to boot, but the fact that them's the rules don't mean I can't ignore them for being dumb.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T08:42:25-07:00","id":234237,"title":"","content":"I would say that even the point of going inside somebody and just using standard attacks might have minimal effects; I'd put a flat cap on how much damage you can inflict in such a form and configuration, regardless of Essence, as a simple matter of available leverage, and in the meantime you're in a fairly hostile environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T08:58:41-07:00","id":234255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233735#post233735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an amazingly self-absorbed and arrogant attitude.<br /> <br /> We know what the books say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just in the last few days, I've been told on various threads that you have to hunt your spirit shape before you can acquire it, that what you're good at has nothing whatever to do with your spirit shape, that the Tell registers as UMI and immediately identifies you as a Lunar, that the Tell can be defeated with First Integrity Excellency, that shapeshifting takes place over 5 ticks, and probably a bunch of other things I'm forgetting.<br /> <br /> Heaven forbid I should think I might know something about these particular rules that maybe others posting on a thread don't. But if anyone was aware of that before, they gave no sign of it. And if a storyteller told me I had to win a grapple in order to change shape, my first thought would be that that storyteller had probably forgotten part of the rules. Because normally, Isidoros can't grapple a Lunar out of changing shape; much less can anyone's stomach muscles.<br /> <br /> If this were ever an issue in a game, I'd probably just say that attempting to change after flying down someone's throat would force your expanding body back up their throat and out their mouth, following the path of least resistance. And/or they get sneezed out or something. But that doesn't eliminate the problem of insta-killing someone from the inside; it just means you can't do it with a shapeshift. And even then, insect form gives Lunars all kinds of crazy advantages. If your target lacks supernatural senses, you don't need to fly inside them to insta-kill them. You can just fly behind them and snap their neck. Or just hang out on the roof of their tent until they fall asleep. You're going to be up all night trying to find ways to eliminate every ridiculous method Lunars can use shapeshifting to kill someone. The best solution is not to have players who are given to use their powers in an abusive or exploitative way in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:12:12-07:00","id":234264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234255#post234255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just in the last few days, I've been told [...] the Tell can be defeated with First Integrity Excellency</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you're either saying that Integrity doesn't contribute to MDV, or that MDV isn't what defeats the tell... hmm... nope.<br /> Even if you couldn't activate the Exc. in response to it, it still does. The situation in which it does would be the only thing to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:22:01-07:00","id":234273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234255#post234255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that what you're good at has nothing whatever to do with your spirit shape</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual conversation was that what you're good at <i>is not necessarily the sole determining factor for the spirit shape</i>. Which they're not. It was in response to the perception that you were insisting a character's Attributes <i>had</i> to line up with the totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:30:59-07:00","id":234283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234273#post234273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actual conversation was that what you're good at <i>is not necessarily the sole determining factor for the spirit shape</i>. Which they're not. It was in response to the perception that you were insisting a character's Attributes <i>had</i> to line up with the totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say they had to line up. I said if they didn't, they needed some other justification for using that spirit shape. They would need to explain how the spirit shape related to them. And yeah, I said if someone's spirit shape's Attributes are the direct opposite of their own as a human, it would have to be a good explanation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234264#post234264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you're either saying that Integrity doesn't contribute to MDV, or that MDV isn't what defeats the tell... hmm... nope.<br /> Even if you couldn't activate the Exc. in response to it, it still does. The situation in which it does would be the only thing to change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean using it in response to the Tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:38:00-07:00","id":234290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234283#post234283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean using it in response to the Tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, that wasn't asserting anything, that was me saying that my ST-at-the-time ruled that way. And he doesn't hang out here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:38:42-07:00","id":234291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234283#post234283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say they had to line up. I said if they didn't, they needed some other justification for using that spirit shape. They would need to explain how the spirit shape related to them. And yeah, I said if someone's spirit shape's Attributes are the direct opposite of their own as a human, it would have to be a good explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's why I said the perception of what you were arguing. I know your position was more nuanced than some took it as being, just as their position was more nuanced than you had presented it a couple of posts up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:48:05-07:00","id":234320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234255#post234255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just in the last few days, I've been told on various threads that you have to hunt your spirit shape before you can acquire it, that what you're good at has nothing whatever to do with your spirit shape, that the Tell registers as UMI and immediately identifies you as a Lunar, that the Tell can be defeated with First Integrity Excellency, that shapeshifting takes place over 5 ticks, and probably a bunch of other things I'm forgetting.<br /> <br /> Heaven forbid I should think I might know something about these particular rules that maybe others posting on a thread don't. But if anyone was aware of that before, they gave no sign of it. And if a storyteller told me I had to win a grapple in order to change shape, my first thought would be that that storyteller had probably forgotten part of the rules. Because normally, Isidoros can't grapple a Lunar out of changing shape; much less can anyone's stomach muscles.<br /> <br /> If this were ever an issue in a game, I'd probably just say that attempting to change after flying down someone's throat would force your expanding body back up their throat and out their mouth, following the path of least resistance. And/or they get sneezed out or something. But that doesn't eliminate the problem of insta-killing someone from the inside; it just means you can't do it with a shapeshift. And even then, insect form gives Lunars all kinds of crazy advantages. If your target lacks supernatural senses, you don't need to fly inside them to insta-kill them. You can just fly behind them and snap their neck. Or just hang out on the roof of their tent until they fall asleep. You're going to be up all night trying to find ways to eliminate every ridiculous method Lunars can use shapeshifting to kill someone. The best solution is not to have players who are given to use their powers in an abusive or exploitative way in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will point out that even under regular MI rules, the rules specifically state that you are aware you are in social combat. Seeing as how there is no option (that I can find, I could be wrong) that allows for an unexpected Social Attack, the character is aware of the social attack the Tell is making, and can spend Integrity on it. Unless the Tell is special in this case as well, like being considered non-magical despite being magical. A character can also use any social combat defenses they want. The alternative is to suggest that you CAN use unexpected social attacks to prevent people from using any defenses. The Tell rules as written are terrible, and make no sense. It just gets worse if you try to make those rules work by putting massive restrictions on how you can defend against social attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:57:42-07:00","id":234329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234320#post234320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will point out that even under regular MI rules, the rules specifically state that you are aware you are in social combat. Seeing as how there is no option (that I can find, I could be wrong) that allows for an unexpected Social Attack, the character is aware of the social attack the Tell is making, and can spend Integrity on it. Unless the Tell is special in this case as well, like being considered non-magical despite being magical. A character can also use any social combat defenses they want. The alternative is to suggest that you CAN use unexpected social attacks to prevent people from using any defenses. The Tell rules as written are terrible, and make no sense. It just gets worse if you try to make those rules work by putting massive restrictions on how you can defend against social attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unexpected social attacks exist (and are hilariously abusable), but even if a character doesn't know a social attack is coming, the player is. Transparancy and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:09:13-07:00","id":234348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234329#post234329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unexpected social attacks exist (and are hilariously abusable), but even if a character doesn't know a social attack is coming, the player is. Transparancy and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Omicron, can you give me a page reference? I've been looking for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:12:59-07:00","id":234356,"title":"","content":"Core, p. 169, under the &quot;Join Battle&quot; header (because fuck proper presentation, right?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unexpected social attacks are quite possible but do not in-volve being physically hidden. Instead, a surprise attack represents an unexpected shift in conversation from innocuous small talk to serious matters. In place of (Dexterity + Stealth), the aggressor conceals his intent with (Manipulation + Socialize), while the defender reflexively counters with (Perception + Investigation).<br /> Reestablishing surprise later in a social engagement requires that the assailant make a completely new point unrelated to the earlier discussion (i.e., changing the subject), which is the equivalent of finding a new place to hide. Otherwise, this miscellaneous action uses the same rules, apart from the dice pools used. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:34:09-07:00","id":234381,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not sure why anyone should think the Tell should be exempt from system transparency tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:37:15-07:00","id":234384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234356#post234356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Core, p. 169, under the &quot;Join Battle&quot; header (because fuck proper presentation, right?)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't help but notice that it doesn't actually say what the effect of a surprise attack is. I can only assume it is the same as regular combat, where your DVs are reduced to 0, and you are not permitted to use any defenses except those that counter a surprise attack. Now, does the Tell count as a surprise attack, because you do not see it coming? This means that all characters are defeated by it with no chance of stopping it unless they use a surprise negator. Or, is it considered an aware attack because you are aware of all attacks except those that make a successful Manipulation + Socialize, and the Tell didn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:56:44-07:00","id":234409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234384#post234384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but notice that it doesn't actually say what the effect of a surprise attack is.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted 2e Core, p. 155</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless a character has a magical means of detecting unexpected attacks (such as Surprise Anticipation Method, on p. 226) or a magical defense that guards against unperceived attacks (as most defensive Charms do), the attack is unblockable and un- dodgeable. That is, the character has a Dodge and Parry DV of 0 automatically, but matters such as cover can improve the value.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same principle there; MDVs are considered zero. Which would mean the 12 MDV is pointless. Meaning the person who wrote the Tell mechanics had no idea how the social combat system worked. <br /> <br /> Unless you can attempt a mundane Perception + Investigation roll (as you can versus mundane social surprise attacks). Which, I mean by the rules you should be able to. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234384#post234384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, does the Tell count as a surprise attack, because you do not see it coming?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it implies that it does in saying it's &quot;undetectable.&quot; A surprise attack is the closet actual mechanical term to this &quot;undetectable&quot; nonsense. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234384#post234384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, is it considered an aware attack because you are aware of all attacks except those that make a successful Manipulation + Socialize, and the Tell didn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not intended to; again, I doubt the author bothered to read the social combat chapter thoroughly before writing the Tell mechanics, and they certainly did not read the rules for surprise attacks and Join Battle that have been cited in this thread.<br /> <br /> Maybe you also assume the Tell got 12 successes on that Manipulation + Socialize roll too. Easy-ish fix. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oramus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234381#post234381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm not sure why anyone should think the Tell should be exempt from system transparency tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's just nonsense to think so. However I do think the extreme degree of system transparency in Exalted hurts the notion of dramatic tension and making tough choices with your IC resources if OOC you always know what is coming at you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:59:37-07:00","id":234410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oramus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234381#post234381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm not sure why anyone should think the Tell should be exempt from system transparency tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, because I don't usually like to know more about someone than my character knows. If someone is a Sidereal or an Infernal or a Lunar and my character has no way of knowing, I don't want to know either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234290#post234290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, that wasn't asserting anything, that was me saying that my ST-at-the-time ruled that way. And he doesn't hang out here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:08:50-07:00","id":234416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234410#post234410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, because I don't usually like to know more about someone than my character knows. If someone is a Sidereal or an Infernal or a Lunar and my character has no way of knowing, I don't want to know either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The baseline mechanics should support some level of seeing surprised IC, rather than the ST having to Rule Zero around them to keep things mysterious.<br /> <br /> However the same logic &quot;you can use Charms to prevent being convinced by a surprise social attack popping out of this letter you received&quot; applies to &quot;you can use Charms to spot the tell&quot; absent a real well-described mechanical distinction between the two.<br /> <br /> And sidenote: I don't believe Resplendent Destinies are treated as social attacks and nothing pops into my mind about Infernals, so I'm not sure what you're referring to when you're talking about Sidereals or Infernals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:32:38-07:00","id":234435,"title":"","content":"Just one thing (in particular, not that there aren't others) that's bugging me in this discussion about Tell mechanics - a magical social attack isn't automatically Unnatural Mental Influence, it's just a social attack that happens because/aided by magic: throwing 20+ dice at a Presence roll is still NMI, rewriting their personality from the ground up is UMI.<br /> <br /> I personally think the Tell should have nothing to do with mental defence values, and go by something to the tune of Perception &amp; Investigation (or Awareness, whatever floats your boat), but be easier to see in false forms rather than true (since your features are already your features 'n all)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/649-nightwinder","name":"Nightwinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:41:35-07:00","id":234445,"title":"","content":"1e tell mechanics ftw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T12:16:55-07:00","id":234524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234445#post234445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e tell mechanics ftw.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> YES!<br /> <br /> [/Bison!]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T17:52:16-07:00","id":234841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234410#post234410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, because I don't usually like to know more about someone than my character knows. If someone is a Sidereal or an Infernal or a Lunar and my character has no way of knowing, I don't want to know either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this an argument against characters of those types having distinguishing details at all, or against characters being able to notice them before they get the full picture.<br /> <br /> I mean, just going by Sidereals, having gold or red or purple as an eye colour in general, and having flecks of stars in their pupils in particular, those have a capacity to be a striking detail to anybody, but one that most characters will have no context to extrapolate from, but many players will be able to figure out fairly quickly. How do you handle that?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T19:00:43-07:00","id":234907,"title":"","content":"Personally I think the easiest answer is to just have the chest Burster Tactic work on Extra's and anything more heroic than that barfs out the growing creature. Frankly I like the idea of using this as an interesting version of stealth and spying, crawl into the sleeping creatures ear, mouth, or nose and you can listen in to what is going on with perception charms before exploding out of the poor miserable extra and then destroying his entire army encampment. Or if you do it quietly with a knack to adopt another human's form you do something like the clone scene from Army of Darkness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T17:10:06-07:00","id":235913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234416#post234416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And sidenote: I don't believe Resplendent Destinies are treated as social attacks and nothing pops into my mind about Infernals, so I'm not sure what you're referring to when you're talking about Sidereals or Infernals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned them as examples because both Sidereals and Infernals have various means of disguising themselves. So do Solars of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=234841#post234841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this an argument against characters of those types having distinguishing details at all, or against characters being able to notice them before they get the full picture.<br /> <br /> I mean, just going by Sidereals, having gold or red or purple as an eye colour in general, and having flecks of stars in their pupils in particular, those have a capacity to be a striking detail to anybody, but one that most characters will have no context to extrapolate from, but many players will be able to figure out fairly quickly. How do you handle that?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a player, I expect to be told whatever my character sees. If I notice someone has oddly colored pupils, I notice someone has oddly colored pupils. Same as if I notice someone is hiding an orichalcum chain shirt under her cloak. Of course, as a player, with setting knowledge, I can sometimes draw more conclusions than a character can. But I still prefer not to be told more than the character can perceive when it isn't necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T17:18:56-07:00","id":235933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=235913#post235913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned them as examples because both Sidereals and Infernals have various means of disguising themselves. So do Solars of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course those are generally supported by mechanics that actually work to do the job they should be doing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If you look for a Solar who is under a Stealth Charm, you have no right to know about the Solar or his Charm unless you manage to see through the magic, if you even can (which is not making any kind of &quot;attack&quot; unlike the Tell).<br /> <br /> It's just a different transparency paradigm when something is phrased as an attack or as combat. Understandably so for the most part, except when someone tries to graft an effect that wants to do X on a system that really was designed only to do A-M.<br /> <br /> The Tell should have just used stealth mechanics. Much more appropriate for what it wants to do than the borked social combat system. Someone tried to get cute with that and it failed miserably. Like, there are Solar Stealth effects that are similar types of &quot;I'm right here but you don't see me because my magic reaches out and stops you from doing so&quot; and they don't even try to use the social combat mechanics to achieve that effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T17:22:45-07:00","id":235937,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the default assumption is that if something opposes your dice pool or static value, you get to know about it as a player in order to use powers that enhance those things. This is one of the real downsides of excellencies -- in 1e, for instance, the only Awareness diceadder was a scenelong effect, so there was no problem with the GM calling for fake Awareness rolls now and then to keep you guessing (as is often done in games where the player rolls to notice things). When the system assumes you're spending per-roll, that feels like cheap mote-baiting, so you really can't get away with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T17:41:34-07:00","id":235961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=235937#post235937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the default assumption is that if something opposes your dice pool or static value, you get to know about it as a player in order to use powers that enhance those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, generally, but you don't need to know everything. For instance, when you meet someone who's disguised, you normally roll (Perception + Awareness). But you don't need to be told that this is a disguise roll. You're just rolling (Perception + Awareness) to see what you notice about this character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=235933#post235933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tell should have just used stealth mechanics. Much more appropriate for what it wants to do than the borked social combat system. Someone tried to get cute with that and it failed miserably. Like, there are Solar Stealth effects that are similar types of &quot;I'm right here but you don't see me because my magic reaches out and stops you from doing so&quot; and they don't even try to use the social combat mechanics to achieve that effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, Solar stealth. IGNORE MEEEE!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T07:34:34-07:00","id":239097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=233726#post233726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Found it for you:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I'd probably resolve that as a type of stunted grapple. If you don't roll enough damage... </i><b>you either can't transform yet,</b><i> or do so in a way that doesn't involve a chestburster.</i></div> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Would it make you feel better if he had said &quot;you have to choose between not transforminging yet, or doing so in a way that doesn't involve a chestburster&quot;? Because that's how I took it. In other words, &quot;can't&quot; from an OOC perspective rather than and IC one. Nothing can stop a Lunar from shapeshifting, but that doesn't mean the player doesn't have to respect limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 08-24-2014, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T07:55:24-07:00","id":239125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/232755-awkward-questions-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=235961#post235961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yes, generally, but you don't need to know everything. For instance, when you meet someone who's disguised, you normally roll (Perception + Awareness). But you don't need to be told that this is a disguise roll. You're just rolling (Perception + Awareness) to see what you notice about this character.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're told to roll Perception + Awareness, it's implicit that you could use an Awareness Excellency or other Charms to improve your roll. There's no division in this case between &quot;actively looking for something&quot; and &quot;instinctively spotting something of interest&quot;; either way when the roll is called for, you can use Charms on it. Meaning that the declarative Charm use is purely an OOC act at least some of the time, versus a deliberate IC act.<br /> <br /> The notion that the Tell's social attack is &quot;undetectable&quot; seems to imply to some that you cannot augment your &quot;notice this thing&quot; pool, in this case the MDV, because you are not aware of the attack IC. Maybe because the MDV is seen as a passive thing, when really it's an averaged result stand-in for a roll that is designed to speed processes up by applying a flat value rather than requiring a roll. But even when applied to other non-deliberate rolls (e.g. Awareness, most Resistance rolls) it's clear that simply OOC being told about something prompts the ability to spend motes to augment it. Hence why the problem arises if there's an implicit &quot;you don't even get an OOC prompt&quot; rule in the Tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}